WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:17.400
Neil Gehrels Swift Observatory, previously called the Swift Gamma-Ray Burst Explorer, was a NASA three-instrument space observatory for studying gamma-ray bursts (GRBs) and monitoring the afterglow in X-ray and UV/visible light at the location of a burst.

00:17.950 --> 00:24.184
It was launched on 20 November 2004, aboard a Delta II launch vehicle.

00:24.814 --> 00:41.266
Headed by principal investigator Neil Gehrels until his death in February 2017, the mission was developed in a joint partnership between Goddard Space Flight Center and an international consortium from the United States, United Kingdom, and Italy.
